{"book":23,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"The Mountain of the Lord","summary":"In the last days all nations stream to God's house in Zion to learn His ways, and weapons become farm tools. Then Isaiah turns to Judah's present, a land full of wealth, horses and idols that the Day of the Lord will bring low.","background":"Verses 2–4 appear almost word for word in Micah 4:1-3. Isaiah and Micah were contemporaries, and scholars debate whether one borrowed from the other or both drew on an earlier oracle. Under King Uzziah, Judah had grown prosperous and strong (2 Chronicles 26:6-15), the wealth Isaiah describes in vv. 7–8.","customs":[{"term":"Ships of Tarshish","verses":"2:16","note":"Large ocean-going merchant ships. Tarshish was a distant port, probably in the far western Mediterranean, so the phrase meant the greatest ships afloat."}],"watchFor":["Swords into plowshares (v. 4); Joel 3:10 turns the image the other way.","The refrain 'the Lord alone shall be exalted in that day' (vv. 11, 17).","Everything lofty is listed for humbling: cedars, mountains, towers, ships (vv. 12–16)."],"connections":["Micah 4:1-3","Joel 3:10","2 Chronicles 26:6-15","Revelation 6:15-16"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["חָזָה","chazah","H2372","HVqp3ms","he saw"],["יְשַׁעְיָהוּ","yesha'yahu","H3470","HNpm","Isaiah"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אָמוֹץ","'amotz","H531","HNpm","Amoz"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["וִירוּשָׁלִָם","virushalim","H3389","HC/Npl","and Jerusalem"]],"x":[[23001001,23001001,7],[23013001,23013001,4],[30001001,30001001,3],[33001001,33001001,3],[35001001,35001001,3]],"xn":5},"2":{"w":[["וְהָיָה","vehayah","H1961","Hc/Vqq3ms","and it will be"],["בְּאַחֲרִית","be'acharit","H319","HR/Ncfsc","at [the] end of"],["הַיָּמִים","haiyamim","H3117","HTd/Ncmpa","the days"],["נָכוֹן","nakhon","H3559","HVNrmsa","est